{title: O God, Our Help in Ages Past}
{artist: Isaac Watts / William Croft}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: C}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: o-god-our-help-in-ages-past.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Our_God_Our_Help_In_Ages_Past-St_Anne) and the Cyber Hymnal score (82% of syllables agree)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Our God, [F]our [C]help [Am]in [Dm]a[G]ges [C]past,
[C]Our [Am]hope [Em]for [Am]years [D]to [G]come,
[G]Our [C]shel[F]ter [Dm]from [G]the [C]stormy [E]blast,
[E]And [Dm]our [C]e[Dm]ter[G]nal [C]home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Under [F]the [C]sha[Am]dow [Dm]of [G]Thy [C]throne
[C]Thy [Am]saints [Em]have [Am]dwelt [D]se[G]cure;
[G]Suf[C]fic[F]ient [Dm]is [G]Thine [C]arm a[E]lone,
[E]And [Dm]our [C]de[Dm]fense [G]is [C]sure.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Before [F]the [C]hills [Am]in [Dm]or[G]der [C]stood,
[C]Or [Am]earth [Em]re[Am]ceived [D]her [G]frame,
[G]From [C]ev[F]er[Dm]last[G]ing [C]Thou art [E]God,
[E]To [Dm]end[C]less [Dm]years [G]the [C]same.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Thy Word [F]com[C]mands [Am]our [Dm]flesh [G]to [C]dust,
[C]Re[Am]turn, [Em]ye [Am]sons [D]of [G]men:
[G]All [C]na[F]tions [Dm]rose [G]from [C]earth at [E]first,
[E]And [Dm]turn [C]to [Dm]earth [G]a[C]gain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[C]A thou[F]sand [C]a[Am]ges [Dm]in [G]Thy [C]sight
[C]Are [Am]like [Em]an [Am]eve[D]ning [G]gone;
[G]Short [C]as [F]the [Dm]watch [G]that [C]ends the [E]night
[E]Be[Dm]fore [C]the [Dm]ris[G]ing [C]sun.
{end_of_verse}
